#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built brick wall"
msgstr "muro di mattoni semi costruito"

#. ~ Description for half-built brick wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Half of a brick wall, looks like it still requires some more resources and "
"effort before being considered a real wall."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "bash!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "brick wall"
msgstr "muro di mattoni"

#. ~ Description for brick wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A solid brick wall, sturdy enough to support a roof with enough walls and "
"keep out any unwanted visitors."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "stone wall"
msgstr "muro di pietra"

#. ~ Description for stone wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A sturdy stone wall."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built stone wall"
msgstr "muro di pietra semi costruito"

#. ~ Description for half-built stone wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Half of a sturdy stone wall.  Some work still needs to be done before this "
"stone wall is complete."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "smoothed rock"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for smoothed rock
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A block of stone that's been smoothed and shaped, commonly granite or marble"
" for funerary chapels and mausoleums."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built adobe wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for half-built adobe wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Half of an adobe brick wall, looks like it still requires some more "
"resources and effort before being considered a real wall."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "adobe wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for adobe wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A solid adobe brick wall, sturdy enough to support a roof with enough walls "
"and keep out any unwanted visitors."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "concrete wall"
msgstr "muro di cemento"

#. ~ Description for concrete wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An aesthetically pleasing design with simple lines, this type of concrete "
"was used with a weaker chemical mixture in order to have faster setting "
"times.  Not ideal for multi-story buildings, but still capable of supporting"
" a roof."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for bulkhead
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned, this wall is "
"capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for underwater bulkhead
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned, this wall is "
"capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  Seems to "
"have sprung a leak, however."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "simple concrete wall"
msgstr "muro di cemento semplice"

#. ~ Description for simple concrete wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A durable and uniform concrete wall, quite drab without decoration.  More "
"than capable of supporting a roof, as well as keeping out most anything, "
"save for vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built simple concrete wall"
msgstr "muro di cemento semplice semi costruito"

#. ~ Description for half-built simple concrete wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A partially poured concrete wall that could probably keep anything behind it"
" quite safe if it were finished."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "reinforced concrete wall"
msgstr "muro di cemento rinforzato"

#. ~ Description for reinforced concrete wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient wall, filled with concrete and rebar.  Best suited "
"for supporting multi-level buildings, only serious explosives and high-speed"
" impacts would be capable of damaging this wall."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "scrrrash!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built reinforced concrete wall"
msgstr "muro di cemento rinforzato semi costruito"

#. ~ Description for half-built reinforced concrete wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Poured concrete with methodically placed rebar sticking out, which isn't "
"practical for supporting roofs or shelter.  It appears to need more "
"resources before being considered complete."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "rebar cage"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for rebar cage
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A structural support system made of rebar that appears to be the early "
"stages of a reinforced concrete wall, just missing the poured concrete."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "simple metal wall"
msgstr "muro di metallo semplice"

#. ~ Description for simple metal wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A relatively simple wall made of scraped together metal.  It's still capable"
" of blocking intruders and supporting a roof with adjacent walls."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built simple metal wall"
msgstr "muro di metallo semplice semi-costruito"

#. ~ Description for half-built simple metal wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A partially built makeshift wall of metal that could potentially support a "
"roof if it were completed."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "screen mesh wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for screen mesh wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A rather flimsy tall wall made of 2x4s and screen mesh, suitable for keeping"
" the bugs out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "wooden wall"
msgstr "muro di legno "

#. ~ Description for wooden wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A finished wall of planks and support beams, capable of supporting an upper "
"level or roof.  Still highly flammable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "chipped wood wall"
msgstr "muro di legna scheggiato"

#. ~ Description for chipped wood wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A wall of aligned two by fours that's starting to crack and break open.  "
"Some cut wood and a number of nails could patch this up quick."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "broken wood wall"
msgstr "muro di legna rotto"

#. ~ Description for broken wood wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A number of planks are missing and the structure is beginning to sag and "
"fall apart.  It's going to need quite a bit of work to repair this wall."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "underwater wooden wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for underwater wooden wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A decaying old section of wooden wall, soaked through and leaking.  It will "
"likely crumble to bits if damaged."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built log wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for half-built log wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A half-constructed wall of notched logs that interlock to provide stability."
"  Needs a few more logs to hold up a roof.  Looks flammable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "log wall"
msgstr "muro di tronchi"

#. ~ Description for log wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A tall wall of timber suitable for housing and insulating from the weather."
"  Quite flammable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "chipped log wall"
msgstr "muro di tronchi scheggiato"

#. ~ Description for chipped log wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A moderately damaged wall, could probably be patched up with some planks and"
" nails."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "broken log wall"
msgstr "muro di tronchi rotto"

#. ~ Description for broken log wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A destroyed wood wall, with only a supporting log left, ready to collapse.  "
"Looks repairable if the damage was replaced and patched together with nails "
"and planks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "palisade wall"
msgstr "palizzata"

#. ~ Description for palisade wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An age-old type of fortification consisting of hefty lumber staked into the "
"ground and cabled together."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "wattle-and-daub wall"
msgstr "muro canna-e-fango"

#. ~ Description for wattle-and-daub wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A relatively primitive wall made by daubing together a lattice of wooden "
"strips using some combination of wet soil, clay, sand, animal dung and "
"straw."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "broken wattle-and-daub wall"
msgstr "muro canna-e-fango rotto"

#. ~ Description for broken wattle-and-daub wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"This wattle-and-daub wall section has been destroyed, leaving mostly just "
"frame, and is barely held together."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built wattle-and-daub wall"
msgstr "muro canna-e-fango semi costruito"

#. ~ Description for half-built wattle-and-daub wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"This wattle-and-daub wall has some of the wooden strip lattice in place, and"
" still requires the rest of the lattice and supporting wet compound to be "
"filled in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "smooth dirt wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for smooth dirt wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A solid wall of compressed dirt, mixed with… something to keep it stable.  "
"Its surface glistens slightly, and it smells like rotten milk."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "heavy rumbling!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "junk metal wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for junk metal wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A wall of rusty scrap metal bolted and wire-tied to a sturdy frame.  Very "
"fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "rammed earth wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for rammed earth wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A solid wall of compressed dirt, sturdy enough to support a roof with enough"
" walls and keep out some unwanted visitors."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "junk metal barrier"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for junk metal barrier
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A short wall of rusty scrap metal bolted and wire-tied to a makeshift frame."
"  Very fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns.  This one isn't quite "
"strong enough to support a roof, but could be reinforced."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "glass wall"
msgstr "muro di vetro"

#. ~ Description for glass wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of glass, it's nothing complicated, and looks extremely "
"fragile.  Some contain glass break sensors or window sensors that trigger if"
" the glass is tampered."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "laminated glass"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for laminated glass
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Laminated glass is composed layers of glass and plastic held together by an "
"interlayer."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "ballistic glass"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "reinforced glass"
msgstr "vetro rinforzato"

#. ~ Description for reinforced glass
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A thicker pane of glass with thin metal wires embedded throughout, "
"strengthening the structural properties.  It's a lot stronger than drywall, "
"but it's not made to support a roof and is weaker than concrete."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "reinforced glass with closed shutters"
msgstr "vetro rifnorzato con persiane chiuse"

#. ~ Description for reinforced glass with closed shutters
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A secondary layer of protection over reinforced glass, these metal shutters "
"are typically used to ward off criminals or protect against damage from "
"extreme weather.  Looks like it can only be opened from the inside.  Even "
"with the installed shutters, it isn't feasible in supporting a roof."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "reinforced glass with open shutters"
msgstr "vetro rinforzato con persiane aperte"

#. ~ Description for reinforced glass with open shutters
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Hanging metal shutters that haven't been deployed, exposing the reinforced "
"glass.  It appears as though the metal shutters can only be activated from "
"the inside."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "metal bars"
msgstr "barre di metallo"

#. ~ Description for metal bars
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Thick, heavy bars from the floor to the ceiling, interlaced wall to wall.  "
"Not made to support roofs, but great for blocking paths."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "paper wall"
msgstr "muro di carta"

#. ~ Description for paper wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A huge wall of pulpy mass, covered in sticky wasp saliva.  You could smash "
"it down effortlessly."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "layered paper wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for layered paper wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A thick wall of layered tree pulp and wasp saliva, hardened to withstand the"
" elements.  You could break through this, but it won't be easy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "root wall"
msgstr "muro di radici"

#. ~ Description for root wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A dirt wall covered with roots."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "wax wall"
msgstr "muro di cera"

#. ~ Description for wax wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A wall made entirely out of wax."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_hardcoded.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_microlab.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_necropolis.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "solid rock"
msgstr "roccia solida"

#. ~ Description for solid rock
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"It's solid rock, could be full of all kinds of interesting things.  Best "
"grab your pickaxe or equivalent digging implement, and strike the earth!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "red stone"
msgstr "pietra rossa"

#. ~ Description for red stone
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A red stone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "green stone"
msgstr "pietra verde"

#. ~ Description for green stone
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A green stone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "blue stone"
msgstr "pietra blu"

#. ~ Description for blue stone
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A blue stone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "iron ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for iron ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed seam of reddish-brown iron ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "banded-iron ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for banded-iron ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed seam of brown-red banded-iron ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "copper ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for copper ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed seam of green copper ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "tetrahedrite ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for tetrahedrite ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed seam of grey tetrahedrite ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "chalcopyrite ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for chalcopyrite ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed seam of light-green chalcopyrite ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "lead ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for lead ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed dull gray and yellow seam of lead ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "galena ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for galena ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed dull gray seam of galena ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "galenau ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for galenau ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed yellow-grey seam of galenau ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "tin ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for tin ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Solid rock, with dark gray hints of what you're fairly certain is an ore of "
"tin."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "coppin ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for coppin ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with a seeming mixture of copper and tin ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "bronzium ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for bronzium ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Solid rock, with a seeming mixture of copper and tin ore. Faintly resembles "
"crude bronze."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "silver ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for silver ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Solid rock, with an exposed gray gleam of silver ore.  There might be a few "
"bits of native silver hidden within, but most of it will need to be "
"processed."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "gold vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for gold vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Hot damn, you've struck gold!  Gleaming through the rock in its native form,"
" it's almost enough to make one forget how much less valuable it is after "
"the end of the world."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "electrumite ore vein"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for electrumite ore vein
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "Solid rock, with an exposed silvered yellow gleam of electrumite ore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "little column"
msgstr "piccola colonna"

#. ~ Description for little column
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A small support column."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built column"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for half-built column
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An empty wooden frame in the shape of a column, built around a concrete and "
"rebar foundation.  It isn't capable of supporting roofs or shelter, and "
"appears to need more resources before being considered complete."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "column"
msgstr "colonna"

#. ~ Description for column
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A concrete column."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "large metal support"
msgstr "grande supporto di metallo"

#. ~ Description for large metal support
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A heavy-duty metal support beam."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "small metal support"
msgstr "piccolo supporto di metallo"

#. ~ Description for small metal support
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A metal support beam."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "field stone wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for field stone wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "A sturdy dry stone wall.  Just rocks fitted together without mortar."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "field stone half-wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for field stone half-wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A half height sturdy dry stone wall.  Just rocks fitted together without "
"mortar.  Complete as is or with extensive work it could be doubled in "
"height."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "pillar"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for pillar
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A concrete column that helps keep the mine's ceiling and walls from "
"collapsing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "wooden fortification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for wooden fortification
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A wooden wall with a firing hole carved out of it, which you can fire "
"through unimpeded if you're adjacent to it.  It doesn't take much out of "
"incoming fire, but it's better than nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "underwater wooden fortification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for underwater wooden fortification
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A waterlogged gunport from the age of sail.  If you have a speargun to fire "
"through it with, it might still serve as light cover against any unexpected "
"encounters with gun-toting sharks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "log fortification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for log fortification
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"Stout timbers with a firing hole carved into it, letting you fire unimpeded "
"if you're adjacent to it.  Provides pretty good cover, but might falter "
"against higher-end firepower."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "field stone fortification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for field stone fortification
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy dry stone wall with a firing hole chiseled out, letting you fire "
"unhindered when adjacent to it.  Basic as it may be, simple stones provide "
"effective cover."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "stone fortification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for stone fortification
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy stone wall with a firing hole chiseled out, letting you fire "
"unhindered when adjacent to it.  An excellent source of cover against "
"anything short of siege weapons."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "brick fortification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for brick fortification
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A solid brick wall with a firing hole built into it, providing an opening to"
" shoot through unimpeded while adjacent to it.  A sturdy source of cover "
"against incoming fire."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "adobe fortification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for adobe fortification
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A solid adobe brick wall with a firing hole built into it, providing an "
"opening to fire through when adjacent to it.  Fairly solid cover against "
"muskets and most small arms alike."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "window"
msgstr "finestra"

#. ~ Description for window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A giant sheet of glass inserted into a window, typically found on the side "
"of shops to showcase goods."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "taped window"
msgstr "finestra sigillata con nastro adesivo"

#. ~ Description for taped window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"Duct tape covers this window, blocking sunlight and visibility.  You could "
"remove the duct tape by cutting it off."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "window with curtains"
msgstr "finestra con tende"

#. ~ Description for window with curtains
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A window with fancy curtains on the inside that can be drawn closed to block"
" visibility and shut out any light."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "You pry open the window."
msgstr "Sei riuscito a forzare la finestra."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "You pry, but cannot pry open the window."
msgstr "Provi a forzare, ma non sei riuscito ad aprire la finestra."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "window without curtains"
msgstr "finestra senza tende"

#. ~ Description for window without curtains
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A smaller window typically found in residential homes.  You could install a "
"curtain rod and drapes if you had the supplies and skill."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "open window without curtains"
msgstr "finestra aperta senza tende"

#. ~ Description for open window without curtains
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A smaller window typically found in residential homes.  It's open and can be"
" crawled through."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for taped window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A smaller window typically found in residential homes.  This one has been "
"blocked out with duct tape.  You could remove the duct tape by cutting it "
"off."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for taped window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"An empty window.  This one has been blocked out with duct tape.  You could "
"remove the duct tape by cutting it off."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "taped glass wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for taped glass wall
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A glass wall.  This one has been blocked out with duct tape.  You could "
"remove the duct tape by cutting it off."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for taped window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A window with fancy curtains on the inside.  This one has been blocked out "
"with duct tape.  You could remove the duct tape by cutting it off."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "open window with curtains"
msgstr "finestra aperta con tende"

#. ~ Description for open window with curtains
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A window with fancy curtains on the inside that can be drawn closed to block"
" visibility and shut out any light.  It's open and you can crawl through."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "window with closed curtains"
msgstr "finestra con tende chiuse"

#. ~ Description for window with closed curtains
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A window with fancy curtains that have been drawn shut, blocking sunlight "
"and visibility.  The curtains can only be opened on the inside.  If you "
"examined the curtains more closely, you could peek through the drapes or "
"tear down everything.  Or you could just smash the window open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for taped window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"Duct tape covers this window, blocking out any sunlight and visibility.  You"
" could remove the duct tape by cutting it off."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "empty window"
msgstr "finestra vuota"

#. ~ Description for empty window
#. ~ Description for empty domestic window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"An empty window frame consisting of two by fours and nails.  You could "
"install a sheet of glass, or even board it up for protection.  You could "
"also convert it into a wall if you took the time to construct it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "empty domestic window"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "window frame"
msgstr "struttura per finestra"

#. ~ Description for window frame
#. ~ Description for domestic window frame
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A wooden window frame that has shattered glass around it.  You'll probably "
"get hurt if you crawled through the sharp and jagged shards.  You could "
"smash out the remaining pieces, or take your time and quietly clean them up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "glass crunching!"
msgstr "vetro che scricchiola!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "domestic window frame"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "boarded up window"
msgstr "finestra barricata"

#. ~ Description for boarded up window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A glass window that has been covered with nailed down planks, blocking "
"sunlight and visibility.  It's not much stronger, but it could be further "
"reinforced with strategically placed two by fours."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for boarded up window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"An empty window frame that has been covered with nailed down planks, "
"blocking sunlight and visibility.  It's not much stronger, but it could be "
"further reinforced with strategically placed two by fours."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "reinforced boarded up window"
msgstr "finestra barricata rinforzata"

#. ~ Description for reinforced boarded up window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A heavily fortified glass window with carefully placed planks across the "
"glass to block vision.  Adding a few spikes and metal plating would further "
"increase its durability."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for reinforced boarded up window
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid ""
"A heavily fortified window with carefully placed planks across the open "
"frame to block vision.  Adding a few spikes and metal plating would further "
"increase its durability."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
msgid "armored boarded up window"
msgstr "finestra barricata corazzata"

