"A large rock, sounds kinda hollow, could crack it open easy enough, wonder "
"whats inside?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "aluminum sulfate"
msgid_plural "aluminum sulfate"
msgstr[0] "solfato di alluminio"
msgstr[1] "solfato di alluminio"
msgstr[2] "solfato di alluminio"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'aluminum sulfate'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several crystals of aluminum sulfate.  Historically, an agent for purifying "
"water and as molluscicide, due to the fact that it degenerates their slime."
"  Just before the Cataclysm, its main uses were for adjusting the acidity of"
" the soil and as an additive to baking powder.  If mixed with a strong acid,"
" it could be used to saturate the soil with aluminum, causing all but the "
"most resistant of plants to wither and die."
msgstr ""
"Diversi cristalli di solfato di alluminio. Storicamente era utilizzato come "
"agente per purificare l'acqua e come pesticida per molluschi grazie "
"all'abilità di degenerare il loro muco. Poco prima il Cataclisma era usato "
"principalmente come correttore dell'acidità del terreno e come additivo al "
"lievito in polvere. Se unito a un forte acido, può essere utilizzato per "
"saturare il terreno in alluminio, facendo appassire tutte le piante, tranne "
"quelle più resistenti."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "acetic acid"
msgid_plural "acetic acid"
msgstr[0] "acido acetico"
msgstr[1] "acido acetico"
msgstr[2] "acido acetico"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'acetic acid'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Concentrated acetic acid, typically used as a chemical reagent and "
"antifungal agent.  Despite its horrid smell, it was used to prepare several "
"types of perfumes, but would making perfume not be too fancy for "
"postapocalyptic New England?"
msgstr ""
"Acido acetico concentrato, tipicamente usato come reagente chimico e agente "
"antifungale. Nonostante l'orrido odore, era usato per preparare diversi tipi"
" di profumi, ma non sarebbe forse non troppo lussuoso creare profumi per la "
"Nuova Inghilterra postapocalittica?"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "formaldehyde"
msgid_plural "formaldehyde"
msgstr[0] "Formaldeide"
msgstr[1] "Formaldeide"
msgstr[2] "Formaldeide"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'formaldehyde'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Formaldehyde, here dissolved in water, was widely used before the Cataclysm "
"as a precursor to production of many chemicals and materials and as an "
"embalming agent.  Easily identifiable by its pungent odor.  Terribly toxic, "
"carcinogenic, and volatile."
msgstr ""
"Il formaldeide, qui dissolto in acqua, era ampiamente usato prima del "
"Cataclisma come un precursore alla produzione di molti agenti chimici e "
"materiali e come un agente di imbalsamazione. Facilmente identificabile dal "
"suo odore pungente. Terribilmente tossico, cancerogeno e volatile."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "thermite"
msgid_plural "thermite"
msgstr[0] "termite"
msgstr[1] "termite"
msgstr[2] "termite"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'thermite'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-greenish powder, produced by mixing aluminum and "
"chromium oxide.  This mixture, burning at a constant pace and at extremely "
"high temperature, was once used for on-the-spot welding.  Can be used as an "
"incendiary material in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Una manciata di una polvere verde-argenteo, prodotta mischiando alluminio e "
"monossido di cromo. Questa mistura poiché brucia a velocità costante e a "
"temperature estremamente alte, era un tempo utilizzata per saldature sul "
"posto. In caso di necessità può essere utilizzata come materiale "
"incendiario."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "ANFO"
msgid_plural "ANFO"
msgstr[0] "ANFO"
msgstr[1] "ANFO"
msgstr[2] "ANFO"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'ANFO'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several brownish pellets that were made by absorbing organic fuel on "
"ammonium nitrate.  This ammonium nitrate-fuel oil or ANFO, as it is called, "
"mixture is a common industrial explosive due to its stability and low price."
"  Burns fast, but needs an explosive primer to detonate."
msgstr ""
"Parecchie palline color marroncino che sono state create facendo assorbire "
"del carburante organico sul nitrato d'ammonio. Questa miscela di carburante "
"all'olio di nitrato d'ammonio, o ANFO, come viene chiamato, è un comune "
"esplosivo industriale a causa della sua stabilità e del suo basso prezzo. "
"Brucia velocemente, ma necessita di un innesco esplosivo per essere "
"detonato."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "black gunpowder"
msgid_plural "black gunpowder"
msgstr[0] "polvere da sparo nera"
msgstr[1] "polvere da sparo nera"
msgstr[2] "polvere da sparo nera"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'black gunpowder'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A handful of black gunpowder, made by mixing charcoal and sulfur with "
"saltpeter.  Pretty useless for making modern cartridges, as the soot "
"produced when it burns will quickly clog any firearm, but it could be used "
"to make some vicious bombs."
msgstr ""
"Una manciata di polvere da sparo nera, prodotta mischiando carbonella e "
"zolfo con salnitro. Abbastanza inutile per produrre cartucce moderne, poiché"
" la fuliggine prodotta quando brucia otturerà rapidamente ogni arma da "
"fuoco, potrebbe essere utilizzata per costruire bombe insidiose."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "match head powder"
msgid_plural "match head powder"
msgstr[0] "polvere di capocchia di fiammifero"
msgstr[1] "polvere di capocchia di fiammifero"
msgstr[2] "polvere di capocchia di fiammifero"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'match head powder'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Some match head powder from match heads, similar to black gunpowder but a "
"bit weaker.  It can be used in crafting explosives and fuses when other more"
" suitable candidates are less available."
msgstr ""
"Della polvere ottenuta dalla capocchia di alcuni fiammiferi. E' simile alla "
"polvere nera, ma ha una reazione più debole. Può essere utilizzata nella "
"produzione di esplosivi e micce quando non si ha altro a disposizione."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "RDX"
msgid_plural "RDX"
msgstr[0] "RDX"
msgstr[1] "RDX"
msgstr[2] "RDX"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'RDX'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Several off-white crystals of RDX or hexogen: a military-grade, shelf-stable"
" high explosive.  Can be cast into shaped charges or mixed with scrap to "
"pepper the blast area with high-velocity shrapnel."
msgstr ""
"Parecchi cristalli color bianco sporco di RDX o esogeno: un esplosivo di "
"grado militare conservabile. Può essere fuso in cariche cave o miscelato con"
" dei rottami per pepare il raggio esplosivo con schegge volanti ad alta "
"velocità."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "composition b"
msgid_plural "composition b"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'composition b'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Composition B is an explosive consisting of castable mixtures of RDX and "
"TNT.  It is used as the main explosive filling in artillery projectiles, "
"rockets, land mines, hand grenades and various other munitions."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "HMTD"
msgid_plural "HMTD"
msgstr[0] "HMTD"
msgstr[1] "HMTD"
msgstr[2] "HMTD"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'HMTD'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Hexamine peroxide: this fine, yellowish powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, but best not store it for too long."
msgstr ""
"Perossido di esamina: questa polvere fine e giallastra è un potente "
"esplosivo primario, usato per innescare la detonazione di esplosivi più "
"stabili, come l'RDX. Relativamente stabile, ma è meglio non conservarlo "
"troppo a lungo."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "improvised rocket fuel"
msgid_plural "improvised rocket fuel"
msgstr[0] "Carburante per razzi improvvisato"
msgstr[1] "Carburante per razzi improvvisato"
msgstr[2] "Carburante per razzi improvvisato"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'improvised rocket fuel'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A chunk of a zinc powder and sulfur mixture, bound together by superglue, "
"that can be used as an impromptu rocket fuel."
msgstr ""
"Un pezzo del composto di polvere di zinco e zolfo, uniti insieme dalla "
"supercolla, che può essere utilizzato come propellente per razzi "
"improvvisato."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "water purification tablet"
msgid_plural "water purification tablets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for water purification tablet
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Intended for the clarification and disinfection of unsafe drinking water, "
"these halazone-based purification tablets remove dangerous contaminants "
"using powerful chemicals.  The label says one tablet purifies up to 2L of "
"water."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "hickory root"
msgid_plural "hickory roots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'hickory root'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A root from a hickory tree.  It has an earthy smell."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "sewage water"
msgid_plural "sewage water"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'sewage water'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Turbid liquid from the sewers with awful stench."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "detergent"
msgid_plural "detergent"
msgstr[0] "Detergente"
msgstr[1] "Detergenti"
msgstr[2] "Detergenti"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'detergent'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A popular pre-Cataclysm washing powder.  It is used for chemistry "
"experiments such as manufacturing gelled gasoline."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "soap flakes"
msgid_plural "soap flakes"
msgstr[0] "Scaglie di sapone"
msgstr[1] "Scaglie di sapone"
msgstr[2] "Scaglie di sapone"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'soap flakes'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A bar of soap cut into flakes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "lye"
msgid_plural "lye"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'lye'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is a liquid form of sodium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive, handle "
"with care."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "nanomaterial canister"
msgid_plural "nanomaterial canisters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'nanomaterial canister'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Steel canisters containing carbon, iron, titanium, copper and other elements"
" in specifically engineered atomic scale configurations.  A nanofabricator "
"can assemble them into usable items."
msgstr ""
"Contenitori di acciaio contenenti carbonio, ferro, titanio, rame ed altri "
"elementi in specialmente ingegnerizzate configurazioni su scala atomica. Un "
"nanofabbricatore può assemblarli in oggetti usabili. "

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "wood ash"
msgid_plural "wood ashes"
msgstr[0] "Cenere di legno"
msgstr[1] "Ceneri di legno"
msgstr[2] "Ceneri di legno"

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wood ash', 'str_pl': 'wood ashes'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is almost weightless residue left after the burning of some substance."
msgstr ""
"Questo è del residuo quasi senza peso della bruciatura di qualche sostanza."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "ether"
msgid_plural "ether"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'ether'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Diethyl ether largely supplanted the use of chloroform as a general "
"anesthetic due to ether's more favorable therapeutic index, that is, a "
"greater difference between an effective dose and a potentially toxic dose."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgid_plural "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Use action activation_message for {'str_sp': 'dimethyl sulfoxide'}.
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "You apply some DMSO."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'dimethyl sulfoxide'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Dimethyl sulfoxide, or DMSO, is a common and important aprotic solvent, "
"capable of dissolving a huge range of things.  It can help many chemical "
"agents diffuse more quickly through the skin, and has a mild analgesic "
"effect on its own."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "chloroform"
msgid_plural "chloroform"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'chloroform'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Famous for its abilities as an illicit sedative, this substance is also a "
"very good solvent.  In particular, it's used a lot in nuclear magnetic "
"resonance spectroscopy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "phenol"
msgid_plural "phenol"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'phenol'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This useful stuff is a potent solvent and has a wide range of reactive "
"applications.  It can be used to make a huge number of plastics and "
"polymers, it can be an antiseptic, it can strip paint and break down epoxy, "
"and it can burn your skin away like tissue paper under a heat gun.  Wear "
"gloves."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "peptone broth powder"
msgid_plural "peptone broth powder"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'peptone broth powder'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is a pre-mixed salty solution of protein and sugar.  It's meant for "
"bacteria to eat, but if you were desperate you could eat it too; it's not "
"much different from cup noodle stock."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "agar"
msgid_plural "agar"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'agar'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"These clear cubes of processed seaweed can be dissolved in boiling water to "
"create a very sturdy, temperature resistant gel.  Not only is it good for "
"making gels to separate molecules by size, but it's a great cheat ingredient"
" to make sure your jellies set properly."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "steel grille"
msgid_plural "steel grilles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'steel grille'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is a metal grille.  It can be used as a framework for making a chemical"
" catalyst."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "cobalt-60 pellet"
msgid_plural "cobalt-60 pellets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'cobalt-60 pellet'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Radioactive material that used to be a part of some nuclear industry "
"equipment.  You are yet to find some use for it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "nuclear waste"
msgid_plural "nuclear waste"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'nuclear waste'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A pellet of silvery metal, still warm to the touch."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "nuclear fuel pellet"
msgid_plural "nuclear fuel pellets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'nuclear fuel pellet'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "A small pellet of fissile material.  Handle carefully."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "wooden bead"
msgid_plural "wooden beads"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'wooden bead'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is a wooden bead.  It can be used to craft inscribable jewelry or "
"create a beaded curtain door."
msgstr ""
"Questa è una perlina di legno. Può essere usata per fabbricare della "
"gioielleria inscrivibile o per creare una porta dalle tende perlate."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "sandbag"
msgid_plural "sandbags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'sandbag'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is a canvas sack filled with sand.  It can be used to construct simple "
"barricades."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "earthbag"
msgid_plural "earthbags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'earthbag'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"This is a canvas sack filled with soil.  It can be used to construct simple "
"barricades."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "rennet"
msgid_plural "rennet"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'rennet'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"Enzymes used to curdle milk, for making cheese.  Traditionally made from the"
" stomachs of ruminant animals."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "acetylene"
msgid_plural "acetylene"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'acetylene'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"A flammable gas that explodes under pressure.  Combined with oxygen, "
"acetylene makes a great welding gas."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid "Shimmer! Floor Wax and Dessert Topping"
msgid_plural "Shimmer! Floor Wax and Dessert Topping"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Shimmer! Floor Wax and Dessert Topping'}
#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
msgid ""
"It's durable and it's scuff resistant!  It even cleans your clothes!  But "
"despite the advertisements, it is not, in fact, delicious."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/containers.json
msgid "2.5L canteen"
msgid_plural "2.5L canteens"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': '2.5L canteen'}
#: data/json/items/containers.json
msgid ""
"A large plastic water canteen, with a 2.5 liter capacity and carrying strap."
msgstr "Una grande borraccia con una capacità di 2,5L e tracolla."

#: data/json/items/containers.json
msgid "power armor 2.5L canteen"
msgid_plural "power armor 2.5L canteens"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'power armor 2.5L canteen'}
#: data/json/items/containers.json
msgid ""
"A large plastic water canteen, with a 2.5 liter capacity.  It's been "
"converted to clip onto power armor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/containers.json
msgid "30 gallon barrel"
msgid_plural "30 gallon barrels"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
